<div class="of-two-column-grid">
    <InfoPanel Title="Week 3 completed foundation"
               Subtitle="The local/free system now proves the business workflow end-to-end."
               Tone="success">

        <ul class="of-mini-list">
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Persistence:</strong>
                <span>SQL Server Express / LocalDB provider support with existing local database fallback.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Local login:</strong>
                <span>Username/email and password login through SQL-backed LocalUsers.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Password storage:</strong>
                <span>Hashed passwords, not plain text.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Session:</strong>
                <span>Persistent local login stores the local user id and reloads roles from SQL.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Roles:</strong>
                <span>Admin, Manager, Reviewer, Worker, and ReadOnly role model.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Permissions:</strong>
                <span>SQL-backed permission matrix for workflow, evidence, reports, exports, settings, and user management.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Evidence:</strong>
                <span>Reusable RecordAttachments component across Work Orders, Corrective Actions, and Document Intake.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Library:</strong>
                <span>Document Library shows active attachments across modules.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Quality:</strong>
                <span>Data Quality flags important records missing supporting evidence.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Reports:</strong>
                <span>Evidence coverage and missing evidence reporting added.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Portfolio docs:</strong>
                <span>Reviewer, demo, business value, technical, integration, scope, and plan pages updated.</span>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </InfoPanel>

    <InfoPanel Title="Week 4 production target"
               Subtitle="The next sprint should add real production integration and permission boundaries."
               Tone="warning">

        <ul class="of-mini-list">
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>OAuth2:</strong>
                <span>Microsoft OAuth2 / Entra ID sign-in.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Account linking:</strong>
                <span>ExternalLoginLinks maps Microsoft account identity to LocalUser.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Authorization:</strong>
                <span>Existing local SQL roles remain the application permission source.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Storage:</strong>
                <span>SharePoint file storage provider through Microsoft Graph.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Configuration:</strong>
                <span>Tenant id, client id, site id, drive/library id, and provider settings.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Testing:</strong>
                <span>Provider swap testing across Work Orders, Corrective Actions, Document Intake, Document Library, Reports, and Activity Log.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Deployment:</strong>
                <span>Local/test/production environment notes, secrets handling, backup/restore, and retention guidance.</span>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </InfoPanel>
</div>

<InfoPanel Title="Week 4 implementation order"
           Subtitle="This order keeps Week 4 focused on production hardening instead of random new pages."
           Tone="default">

    <div class="of-review-proof-grid">
        <div class="of-review-proof-card">
            <span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Step 1</span>
            <h3>Configuration foundation</h3>
            <p>
                Add appsettings/user-secrets/environment variable structure for OAuth2, Graph, SharePoint, storage provider, and environment boundaries.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="of-review-proof-card">
            <span class="of-badge of-badge-warning">Step 2</span>
            <h3>Microsoft OAuth2</h3>
            <p>
                Add Microsoft login and callback flow without breaking the local/free login fallback.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="of-review-proof-card">
            <span class="of-badge of-badge-success">Step 3</span>
            <h3>Account linking</h3>
            <p>
                Map Microsoft identity claims to ExternalLoginLinks, then resolve the matching LocalUser.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="of-review-proof-card">
            <span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Step 4</span>
            <h3>Role policy enforcement</h3>
            <p>
                Use the LocalUser roles and LocalRolePermissions as the app authorization source after OAuth2 sign-in.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="of-review-proof-card">
            <span class="of-badge of-badge-warning">Step 5</span>
            <h3>SharePoint storage provider</h3>
            <p>
                Implement the provider behind IFileStorageService using Microsoft Graph without rebuilding workflow pages.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="of-review-proof-card">
            <span class="of-badge of-badge-muted">Step 6</span>
            <h3>Production readiness docs</h3>
            <p>
                Document tenant setup, app registration, permission scopes, site/library setup, folder convention, and deployment boundaries.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="of-review-proof-card">
            <span class="of-badge of-badge-success">Step 7</span>
            <h3>Final release packaging</h3>
            <p>
                Update README, screenshots, release notes, known limitations, and the reviewer walkthrough path.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</InfoPanel>

<InfoPanel Title="Critical implementation rule"
           Subtitle="Week 4 should keep the Week 3 business workflow and replace the infrastructure underneath it."
           Tone="info">

    <div class="of-link-row">
        <span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Login</span>
        <span>→</span>
        <span class="of-badge of-badge-success">LocalUser</span>
        <span>→</span>
        <span class="of-badge of-badge-warning">Role permissions</span>
        <span>→</span>
        <span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Record details</span>
        <span>→</span>
        <span class="of-badge of-badge-success">Upload evidence</span>
        <span>→</span>
        <span class="of-badge of-badge-warning">Document Library</span>
        <span>→</span>
        <span class="of-badge of-badge-danger">Data Quality</span>
        <span>→</span>
        <span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Reports</span>
        <span>→</span>
        <span class="of-badge of-badge-muted">Activity Log</span>
    </div>

    <p class="of-muted-text">
        Work Orders, Corrective Actions, Document Intake, Document Library, Data Quality, Reports, and Activity Log should not be rebuilt for SharePoint.
        The production implementation should replace the provider/authentication layer underneath the existing workflow.
    </p>
</InfoPanel>

<GuidanceNote Title="Current sprint decision" Icon="🏁" Tone="success">
    <p>
        Finish Week 3 with local SQL authentication, persistent login, role documentation, storage readiness, release notes, screenshots,
        and a clean Git status before starting Week 4.
    </p>
</GuidanceNote>